# Architecture Plan

## Scope for issues #75-#79
- Replace the remaining Matter.js lesson simulation stack with deterministic SVG pulley diagrams and a shared pulley-state hook.
- Move force and mechanical-advantage readouts onto derived state instead of runtime physics values.
- Migrate lessons 1-5 and home/lesson embedded demos off `SimulationCanvas`.
- Remove obsolete physics modules and replace the current engine regression coverage with geometry and ratio tests.

## Current module ownership to replace
```text
src/
  components/simulation/
    simulation-canvas.tsx
    simulation-canvas-runtime.tsx
    compare-simulations.tsx
  lib/simulation/
    pulleys.ts
    drag-interactions.ts
    force-overlay.ts
    rope-renderer.ts
    engine-regression.test.ts
  components/home/
    home-force-demo.tsx
    home-compare-demo.tsx
    home-hero-simulation-demo.tsx
  components/lessons/
    *-runtime.tsx and Matter-backed lesson widgets
  components/readouts/
    force-meter.tsx
    mechanical-advantage.tsx
```

## Target module structure
```text
src/
  lib/pulley/
    pulley-geometry.ts       # tangentPoints, arcSweep, ropePath
    pulley-types.ts          # shared config and derived-state types
    use-pulley-state.ts      # pull/load/MA state hook
  components/pulley/
    pulley-diagram.tsx       # SVG renderer + drag interaction + context
    pulley-context.ts        # readout/context bridge
  components/readouts/
    force-meter.tsx
    mechanical-advantage.tsx
  components/home/
    home-hero-pulley-diagram.tsx
    home-force-demo.tsx      # rewritten to SVG/state model
    home-compare-demo.tsx    # rewritten compare view if still needed
  components/lessons/
    lesson widgets rewritten around PulleyDiagram
  tests
    pulley-geometry.test.ts
    use-pulley-state.test.ts
    pulley-diagram.test.tsx (only if needed for drag behavior smoke)
```

## Shared types and contracts
- Introduce a single pulley configuration shape shared by geometry, hook, and component layers:
  - `PulleyType = "fixed" | "movable" | "compound"`
  - `PulleyConfig`
    - `type`
    - `pulleyCount`
    - `loadWeight`
    - `maxPullDistance`
    - optional sizing/layout tokens for the SVG renderer
- Introduce a derived state shape returned by `usePulleyState(config)`:
  - `pullDistance`
  - `loadDistance`
  - `mechanicalAdvantage`
  - `forceNeeded`
  - `setPull(nextDistance)`
  - `reset()`
- `ropePath(...)` should be pure and accept only already-derived geometry inputs so it remains snapshot-testable and reusable in both the main diagram and any small preview variants.
- `<PulleyDiagram>` should provide the derived state through context so `ForceMeter` and `MechanicalAdvantage` can consume it without prop-drilling.

## Key design decisions
- Replace simulation with deterministic math end-to-end. No hybrid mode: once issue #78 lands, Matter.js should be gone from app code and tests.
- Keep geometry pure and serializable. All path building, tangent math, and ratio calculations should live in `src/lib/pulley`, not inside React components.
- Model mechanical advantage directly from pulley configuration rather than inferred from motion:
  - fixed pulley: `MA = 1`
  - movable pulley: `MA = 2`
  - compound pulley: `MA` derived from supported rope segments / configured pulley count
- Keep drag interaction in SVG/pointer space with one clamped source of truth: dragging updates `pullDistance`, and everything else derives from that.
- Preserve existing readout visuals where possible; only the data source changes.
- Remove old Matter-based fixtures instead of adapting them. That keeps the migration clean and reduces dead compatibility code.

## Issue dependency map
1. `#75 Pulley geometry primitives & usePulleyState hook`
   - foundation for all following work
   - creates pure math/state layer
2. `#76 <PulleyDiagram> SVG component with drag interaction`
   - depends on `#75`
   - introduces context and user interaction surface
3. `#77 Adapt <ForceMeter> and <MechanicalAdvantage> to the new state hook`
   - depends on `#75`
   - should integrate cleanly with the context added in `#76`
4. `#78 Migrate lessons 1-5 to <PulleyDiagram> and remove the Matter.js engine`
   - depends on `#75-#77`
   - largest surface-area change, deletes old simulation modules
5. `#79 Geometry & ratio tests; remove obsolete physics tests`
   - depends on all previous issues
   - finalizes the migration by replacing engine tests with geometry/state coverage

## Recommended implementation order
1. Build the pure geometry/state layer in `src/lib/pulley`.
2. Add `<PulleyDiagram>` and its context bridge, but keep old lesson widgets untouched until the API feels stable.
3. Repoint `ForceMeter` and `MechanicalAdvantage` to either explicit derived props or context-backed values from `<PulleyDiagram>`.
4. Migrate reusable home/lesson widgets one by one, starting with the simplest fixed-pulley scenes and ending with Lesson 4's challenge and any compare/gallery variants.
5. Delete Matter-specific runtime modules, imports, and test fixtures once no route or lesson references them.
6. Add geometry and ratio tests, then remove the obsolete Matter regression tests in the same change set so the suite reflects the new architecture only.
